Also `mocks.when(...).thenThrow(...)` — `thenThrow` exists on `fflib_StubbingState`/OngoingStubbing in the library; canonical in fflib samples. And `mocks.getMock(Type)`? Not certain either — I already decided to keep local references from `mocks.mock(...)` and pass them around. I re-introduced `getMock` by habit; `fflib_ApexMocks` does not expose `getMock`. Final fix: keep the mock instances as static test-scoped variables set by `injectMocks()`.

